# Safety net only — NOT the mechanism that defines the publish set.
#
# The publish set is defined by `python scripts/publish_site.py`, which copies
# git-tracked files into dist/ and nothing else. Always deploy dist/:
#
#     nsyte deploy ./dist ...
#
# Why dist/ and not the repo root:
#
# 1. The working-tree art/ is ~2.8 GB of source material (renders, references,
#    video intros, world-plate originals). Only ~62 MB of it is git-tracked and
#    only ~20 MB is actually referenced by the pages. A repo-root deploy would
#    try to upload all of it.
# 2. art/cards/node-runner-web/manifest.json carries 297 SHA-256 fields, which
#    the nsyte secrets scanner reports as "297 potential private keys" and which
#    aborts a non-interactive deploy. This was observed live on 2026-08-09, and a
#    root .nsyte-ignore did NOT suppress it. dist/ never contains that file, so
#    the finding cannot occur — exclusion by construction rather than by rule.
#
# The patterns below therefore exist to blunt the damage if someone deploys the
# repo root by mistake. Do not rely on them; they are the belt, dist/ is the
# braces.

# The sha256 manifest that trips the secrets scanner (see note 2 above).
manifest.json

# Source material and build output that must never be published.
art/
!art/brand/
!art/fonts/
!art/resources/
!art/rulebook/
!art/world-plates/
!art/cards/

# Server state: SQLite match database, seat tokens, WAL/SHM sidecars.
server/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Repo scaffolding with no place on a static site.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.audit/
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
scripts/
tests/
docs/
rules/
cards/
*.py
*.toml
*.lock
uv.lock
package.json
package-lock.json
.env
